  "body": "## Required behavior\n\nWhen adaptive negotiation reaches `maxAutomaticOffer`, Flipbot must **not** stop the configured ladder. It must continue through every remaining configured step using the same capped price, while preserving that step's own message and response policy.\n\nExample:\n\n- configured prices: 1000 / 1100 / 1200 / 1300 / 1400\n- `maxAutomaticOffer = 1200`\n- effective prices: 1000 / 1100 / 1200 / 1200 / 1200\n- messages: step 1 / step 2 / step 3 / step 4 / step 5 respectively\n\n## Fix\n\n- Adaptive pricing now clamps a calculated next price to the global cap instead of returning no next step.\n- Once the current real offer already equals the cap, later configured steps stay on that exact price.\n- Same-price next steps are permitted only for this adaptive-cap plateau. Lower prices and same-price steps below the cap still fail closed.\n- Configured step number, message and response policy are preserved.\n- A configuration cap lowered below an already-sent offer still fails closed; Flipbot never lowers an active offer automatically.\n- The bot form now explains the plateau behavior explicitly.\n\n## Regression coverage\n\n- calculated next offer above cap -> capped next step is still generated;\n- step 3 at 1200 -> step 4 at 1200 with message 4;\n- step 4 at 1200 -> step 5 at 1200 with message 5;\n- decision service sends the capped next step instead of marking the negotiation rejected;\n- equal-price offers are accepted only when current/next price both equal the active adaptive cap.\n",
